[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561226 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fab4792-0fe1-5a5c-8754-509af469da68" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Number of Intersection Points of Two Lines" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050240 :topic/title "Systems of Equations With No Solutions and Infinitely Many Solutions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15c788b1-e8d1-5ab2-b2ec-c639e5a5f429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561196} {:answer/id #uuid "78dd7c65-7c23-5532-976d-ff5e37ca8e9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at one point" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561224} {:answer/id #uuid "7f8afa02-2884-5634-93a8-7b7ccd61ae05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "intersect at infinitely many points" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15c788b1-e8d1-5ab2-b2ec-c639e5a5f429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "do not intersect" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561196} :answer-field/id #uuid "486aff25-f9b1-5424-a420-03217a3f6814" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7990b398-b163-5ff0-bd59-3b73f685ea5d" :question/problem "Consider the lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$, defined as\n$l_{1}: -4x + y = 2, l_{2}: -12x + 3y =-15$.\n\nAt how many points do these lines intersect?\n\nThe lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$ {{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The number of points of intersection between the two lines is equal to the number of solutions of the corresponding system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4x + y &= 2 \\\\ -12x + 3y &=-15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve the system using substitution. First, we solve for $y$ in the first equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-4x + y &= 2 \\\\\ny &= 4x + 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute\n\n$$\ny=4x + 2\n$$\n\ninto the second equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-12x + 3y &=-15 \\\\\n-12x + 3\\left(4x + 2\\right) &= -15 \\\\\n-12x + 12x + 6 &= -15 \\\\\n6 &= -15\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe result is a statement that's always false. Therefore, we conclude that the system has no solutions.\n\nConsequently, the lines do not intersect (i.e., they are parallel)."}]
